<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Shortfall - accounting quality, S&amp;P 500 and ASX 200</title>
<meta name="description" content="Companies whose accounting quality is deteriorating, and the specific flag that fired. A flag is not a thesis.">
<meta property="og:type" content="website">
<meta property="og:title" content="Shortfall">
<meta property="og:description" content="Companies whose accounting quality is deteriorating, and the specific flag that fired.">
<meta property="og:url" content="https://charlietrenorden.com/shortfall/">
<meta property="og:image" content="https://charlietrenorden.com/shortfall/og.png">
<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
<link rel="icon" href="favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml">
<link rel="icon" href="favicon-192.png" type="image/png" sizes="192x192">
<script>
  /* set theme before paint to avoid a flash - same key as the hub */
  (function () {
    try {
      var saved = localStorage.getItem("theme");
      var dark = saved ? saved === "dark"
        : !(window.matchMedia && window.matchMedia("(prefers-color-scheme: light)").matches);
      document.documentElement.setAttribute("data-theme", dark ? "dark" : "light");
    } catch (e) { document.documentElement.setAttribute("data-theme", "dark"); }
  })();
</script>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
<script defer src="https://static.cloudflareinsights.com/beacon.min.js" data-cf-beacon='{"token": "32b821209b5441a08df42ccf61c9e6c2"}'></script>
</head>
<body>
<div class="page">
  <div class="bar">
    <a class="home" href="https://charlietrenorden.com/"><span class="back">&larr;</span>&nbsp;Other projects</a>
    <button class="toggle" id="themeBtn" type="button" aria-label="Toggle light and dark theme"><span class="dot"></span><span id="themeLbl">Dark</span></button>
  </div>

  <header class="hero">
    <h1>Shortfall</h1>
    <p class="lede">Six accounting tests over the S&amp;P 500 and ASX&nbsp;200.
    Every company scored against its sector peers. Higher is worse.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="panel" id="quadPanel" aria-label="Score against short interest">
    <div class="panel-head">
      <h2>Cross-Plot</h2>
      <label class="xpick"><select id="yvar"></select> against <select id="xvar"></select></label>
      <p class="note" id="quadNote"></p>
    </div>
    <svg id="quadSvg" role="img" aria-label="Score against short interest"></svg>
    <p class="chartkey" id="quadKey"></p>

  </section>

  <section class="panel" id="stripPanel" aria-label="Where each company sits on each test">
    <div class="panel-head">
      <h2>Distributions</h2>
      <p class="note" id="stripNote"></p>
    </div>
    <div id="strips"></div>
  </section>

  <section class="panel" id="weights">
    <div class="panel-head">
      <h2>Weighting</h2>
      <p class="note">Weighted by how directly each test observes an accounting
      problem. Move one and cards show the default alongside.</p>
    </div>
    <div id="sliders"></div>
    <button id="resetWeights" type="button">Reset</button>
  </section>

  <section class="panel" id="filterPanel">
    <div id="filters"></div>
  </section>

  <nav class="pager top" id="pagerTop" aria-label="Result pages">
    <button type="button" id="prevPageTop" aria-label="Previous page">&larr;</button>
    <span id="pageInfoTop"></span>
    <button type="button" id="nextPageTop" aria-label="Next page">&rarr;</button>
  </nav>

  <div id="testHead" aria-label="Filter each test"></div>

  <section id="cards"></section>

  <nav class="pager" id="pager" aria-label="Result pages">
    <button type="button" id="prevPage" aria-label="Previous page">&larr;</button>
    <span id="pageInfo"></span>
    <button type="button" id="nextPage" aria-label="Next page">&rarr;</button>
  </nav>

  <div id="tip" role="tooltip"></div>

  <section class="panel" id="explain">
    <h2>The Tests</h2>
    <div class="tablewrap">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Test</th>
            <th>What it is</th>
            <th>Bear reading</th>
            <th>Bull reading</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody id="explainBody"></tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="panel" id="limits">
    <h2>Caveats</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No backtest. Score against 12-month return is rho 0.01, on one year of
      {{ names|length }} names. That is too small to detect an effect this size either
      way.</li>
      <li>The {{ disclosed|length }} companies that restated or lost an auditor sit at a
      median rank of 291 of {{ names|length }}. Short interest picked them up; these
      tests did not.</li>
      <li>Filing events are US only. The {{ counts.get("Australia (ASX)", 0) }}
      Australian names cannot carry them.</li>
      <li>Australian cash flow is derived from two routes. Where they disagree the
      accruals test is dropped.</li>
      <li>Inventory is scaled by revenue, not cost of sales.</li>
      <li>{{ excluded|length }} companies are unranked, with fewer than three applicable
      tests. Not applicable is not a pass.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="fineprint">SEC EDGAR for the United States, Yahoo Finance for Australia,
    as filed. Not investment advice.</p>
  </section>

  <footer>
    <a href="https://charlietrenorden.com/">charlietrenorden.com</a>
  </footer>
</div>
<script src="data.js"></script>
<script src="app.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
